Tropical Reinforcement Learning contains an adaptation of RAGEN-2. The original RAGEN MIT
license and copyright notice are retained in LICENSE.
Upstream: https://github.com/mll-lab-nu/RAGEN

The vendored verl/verl runtime is from VERL v0.6.1, revision
 d62da4950573d7a4b7ef2362337952e7ab59e78d.
Upstream: https://github.com/volcengine/verl
Its Apache-2.0 license is retained in verl/LICENSE, together with the
copyright and license headers in the source files. Documentation, examples,
tests, build artifacts, and Git history are omitted from this runtime snapshot.

The WebShop simulator and bundled small catalog/search indexes are from
webshop-minimal, revision 4758174947e5494f0cda3b762508ed4a20a2e4cf.
Upstream: https://github.com/ZihanWang314/webshop-minimal
Original environment: https://github.com/princeton-nlp/WebShop
The upstream adaptation credits Xing Jin and Zihan Wang. The pinned package
metadata declares MIT licensing but does not contain a LICENSE file; this
release does not add or replace an upstream license statement.
The simulator's runtime, templates, bundled data, indexes, and requirements
are preserved. These are environment resources, not experiment results.

Third-party credits identify upstream software, not the anonymous submission
authors. Model weights and external datasets are downloaded separately and
remain subject to their respective terms.

The vendored runtimes use minimal local packaging metadata so installation
does not require the omitted upstream README files or example directories.
Runtime source and legal headers are otherwise preserved.
